# Asahi: Add support for GL_EXT_memory_object[_fd] for OpenGL-Vulkan interop.
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/42872 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?

This implements support for GL_EXT_memory_object[_fd], usable for typical OpenGL-Vulkan interop, so OpenGL (asahi) and Vulkan (hk) can exchange color, depth and stencil buffers, and synchronize meaningfully.

It has been tested so far on M2 Pro with Psychtoolbox-3 (OpenGL->Vulkan direction) and Hans-Kristian's Granite toolkits gl_interop_test (Vulkan->OpenGL direction) for rendering and display, and for VR use cases with the Monado XR OpenXR runtime, and Psychtoolbox-3 (as XR client) as well as openxr-playground (as XR client) for OpenGL OpenXR clients using XR_KHR_opengl_enable to transfer color and depth buffers between the OpenGL XR client and Vulkan based XR compositor.

Additionally, all the relevant piglit tests for spec/external_objects now pass, as well as gl-cts test cases.

Iow. the current functionality is usable for various real world use cases, at least the ones I know.
